 "notes": "OWNER 25 Oct: replace the existing deck in the same footprint, built-in benches included. Diamond Piers; TrueFrame pressure-treated frame; 6x6 Douglas fir rough posts; Fulton rail on the 'R' edges; TimberTech Terrain+ Dark Oak; single picture frame, NO butt joints, divider boards (3 sections of full boards; dividers on the gutter and on the trim right of the door, roughly 13' each side); CONCEALoc hidden fasteners in the field, Cortex for the picture frame, benches and stairs. Stairs: 3 risers out the center front; the left side is open, no rail, at grade \u2014 as low as possible, one 4'-wide riser if code needs it. SKETCH (inches, house at top): left lobe 68 / 73 / 68 / 73 / 54, 170 deep; center 94 front at 134 deep; right lobe 50 / 73 / 71 / 70 / 72 back to the house; overall 34'-6\". Read: 45-degree-ish facets solved so the depths close at 170 / 134 and the width closes at 414\". OWNER 25 Oct (pricing): 40% margin; dumpster + toilet $800; no general conditions or site services. No roof covers. OWNER 25 Oct (later): rail ONLY where the sketch has a blue R (73\" bottom-left, 54\", center front beside the stair, 50\", 73\" bottom-right, 71\"); open where nothing is noted (73\" left side, 68\" bottom-left angle); planter on the 68\" top-left angle at the house (17\" x 17\" x the side, treated 2x4 @ 12\" OC with plates, OSB, deck board all sides, picture-frame cap, ~$2,500); benches on the 70\" right side and the 72\" angle at the bay (17\" high, 17\" deep, 4x4 posts wrapped in deck board, ~$3,000 per section). No concrete pad. Client is an accountant \u2014 precise, no guessing. Alternate requested: White Impression Rail Express, vertical infill, modern top rail. SITE (Arapahoe County / City of Centennial GIS, 25 Oct): AIN 2073-15-2-12-013, Lot 12 Blk 1 Jackson Farm Sub 3rd Flg, 7,549 SF, NC6 zoning, built 1993, rear faces east (90.5 deg); assessor sketch: rear wall 44' incl. a 2' x 14' bump at the south corner, 1st-floor box bay 10' wide x 2' (2' angled sides) 22'-32' from the south corner; no deck permit on record. County 3\" orthos 2012-2024 confirm 34'-6\" overall and the center-front corners at 13'-5\" / 21'-3\" within the image resolution. FIT 25 Oct: the field outline matches the existing rails in the county orthos to ~1\" rms (2016/2018) with no scaling; the house sits 1.96 deg off the lot lines; the nearest point (right lobe front corner) is ~17.1' (+/-0.3') from the rear lot line. PHOTO MEASURE (photo 2, projective fit on the wall plane): door opening 17.3'-20.3' from the deck's left end, downspout 16.2', column right of the door 20.5'-21.25' (= the bay's left end), lower window 3-lite trim 5.6'-14.4'. DESIGN READS: dividers at the center-front corners (13'-5\" / 7'-10\" / 13'-3\") \u2014 the right one lands on the trim right of the door; the downspout is 2'-10\" right of the left one (on it, the divider would land in the stair opening). Deck surface stays at the existing elevation (door step kept, 3 risers out front); the left side's grade must drop ~5\" for the 2x10 frame + fascia, so a 4'-wide box step (2 risers @ 6\") goes on the 73\" left side. OWNER 26 Oct: 'first fix the house' \u2014 first floor rebuilt from photos 2 / 4 / q01-q10: 3-lite family-room window and the bay windows with white plantation shutters behind the glass, the back door with its black security storm door (scroll bands top and middle), coach lantern left of the casing, column right of the door, GFCI outlet, window well with its black cover. 'Deck color way off \u2014 light brown caramel, not dark brown': TimberTech's own product swatch samples to a medium taupe-caramel (median #73624a); the old palette (#5c4838) was far too dark \u2014 re-sampled for all three Terrain+ colours (engine + skill). Terrain+ is a scalloped profile (TimberTech FAQ) and CORTEX-compatible. STAIRS: the left side is a 4'-wide framed box step (2 risers @ 6-3/16\", 12.4\" to the reset brick border), the centre stair gets stepped Terrain+ fascia skirts both sides. YARD (photos + 2016/2024 orthos): lawn falls ~1.4' south to north (BvC 3-5%), 2-4 course tumbled-block retaining wall + raised mulch bed around the right lobe (multi-stem tree, window well), single-course block edging + ground cover around the left lobe front, brick border on the open left edges, flagstones on the south side, spruces and a big deciduous tree near the rear lot line, cedar fences on the lot lines. The yard trees shade the deck until ~11:30 in late summer; renders at 15 Sep, noon. ALTERNATE: White Impression Rail Express (3\" posts, universal baluster panels, Modern top rail) on the same R sides \u2014 $120/LF rule vs Fulton $85/LF: +$1,134. FLAGS: the brick border on the open left edges must come up and be reset ~5\" lower for the new frame (not in the price); left divider 2'-9\" left of the downspout (on it, it would land in the stair opening); IRX: confirm with Henry whether the $275.52 section includes the Modern top rail (carried separately at $92 est.).",
